{"description":"Rehire one worker from an ended contract as a NEW ADMIN_BALANCE-funded contract with an ACTIVE_FUNDED qualification milestone. Preserves the ended contract and historical proposal. Zero money moves during rehire; later release remains human-only. Reuses the canonical Job Messages conversation and converges current new-hire Project To-dos/integrations. Fails closed on active contracts, stale lineage, open money or a dispute on any contract of the job + worker (funded or unreleased milestones, milestones under review or with unresolved refunds, unsettled payouts, pending approvals, disputed time, timesheets awaiting review), an ended contract whose tracker enrollment is neither revoked nor carried (PROVIDER_OFFBOARDING_PENDING: a live, error-free membership on the path contract is carried instead; a pending, errored or uncarried one blocks; retry after the old offboarding confirms the revocation), cross-tenant targets, or missing canonical-admin authority. Request-bound and generation-scoped idempotency, the same as the REST operation, prevents duplicate contracts. The `carryOver` report in the response lists every item the NEW contract carried (still-valid identity checks, agreements signed on unchanged content, to-dos completed on the same version, training courses completed on the same course version under the same modules and completion policy with their completed lessons but never attempts or answers, a live tracker membership on the same project with zero provider calls, the Job DM), reset with a reason, skipped or blocked, plus `humanActions` a person still needs to take; it is fixed when the rehire commits. Besides the legacy `provisioning` fields, the response carries a live `onboarding` receipt for the NEW contract (exact assignment readback, durable hook state, provider provisioning state; recomputed on every replay): `onboarding.status` COMPLETE is the only full success \u2014 PENDING, RETRYABLE_FAILED, or terminal FAILED is a PARTIAL SUCCESS: for PENDING/RETRYABLE_FAILED retry this tool with the SAME idempotencyKey to re-heal and re-check; for FAILED (error.retryable=false) follow error.remediation instead (a same-key retry cannot heal it); read opentrain_list_project_todos for the new contract when you need current assignment truth.","execution":{"taskSupport":"forbidden"},"inputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"amountUsd":{"description":"Milestone amount in USD.","exclusiveMinimum":0,"type":"number"},"description":{"description":"Milestone description.","minLength":1,"type":"string"},"dueDate":{"description":"Optional ISO-8601 due date.","minLength":1,"type":"string"},"idempotencyKey":{"description":"Request-bound idempotency key (1-128 chars of letters, digits, dot, underscore, dash, colon). The same key with the same payload converges on the original result; reusing a key with a changed payload conflicts.","pattern":"^[A-Za-z0-9._:-]{1,128}$","type":"string"},"name":{"description":"Optional milestone name.","minLength":1,"type":"string"},"priorContractId":{"description":"Ended OpenTrain contract id to chain the new contract from.","minLength":1,"type":"string"}},"required":["idempotencyKey","description","amountUsd","priorContractId"],"type":"object"},"name":"opentrain_create_admin_balance_rehire","outputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"apiBaseUrl":{"type":"string"},"result":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"carryOver":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"contractId":{"type":"string"},"humanActions":{"items":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"itemId":{"type":"string"},"kind":{"enum":["WORKER_VERIFY_IDENTITY_OR_LOCATION","WORKER_SIGN_AGREEMENT","WORKER_ACCEPT_INTEGRATION_INVITE","OPERATOR_REVIEW_PROVIDER_ENROLLMENT"],"type":"string"},"provider":{"type":"string"}},"required":["kind"],"type":"object"},"type":"array"},"items":{"ite